00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.420
Deep learning algorithms have a huge hunger for training data. They just often work best

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.540
when you can find enough labeled training data to put into the training set. This has

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:15.180
resulted in many teams sometimes taking whatever data you can find and just shoving it into

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:19.980
the training set just to get more training data, even if some of this data or even

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.740
maybe a lot of this data doesn't come from the same distribution as your depth and test

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:30.340
data. So in the deep learning era, more and more teams are now training on data that

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.080
comes from a different distribution than your depth and test sets. And there's some

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.420
subtleties and some best practices for dealing with when you train and test

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.020
distributions differ from each other. Let's take a look. Let's say that you're

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:49.900
building a mobile app where users will upload pictures taken from the cellphones

